## What is included

- self-contained Windows x64 WinUI 3 / .NET 10 desktop package
- native read-only-first ISO/VHD/VHDX Mount + Unmount path
- Dragon Explorer navigation, search, preview and safe Copy out for proven mounted/direct-browse paths
- managed ISO9660/Joliet direct browsing without a native mount
- image Analyze reporting with text/JSON output and JSON export
- SHA-256 + SHA-512 verification
- shared-Core read-only automation CLI
- reversible per-user Windows Open With/context-menu helper
- exact capability documentation generated from the canonical provider registry

The release includes `SUPPORTED-CAPABILITIES-{{VERSION}}.md`, a snapshot of the source-derived provider capability matrix used during release preparation. The maintained repository copy remains under `docs/SUPPORTED-CAPABILITIES.md`.

Capability-matrix SHA-256 used during release preparation: `{{CAPABILITY_MATRIX_SHA256}}`.

## Important capability boundaries

- Provider `Inspect` support does not imply arbitrary filesystem extraction, mounting or writing.
- QCOW2 and hosted-sparse VMDK guest-byte access is limited to the explicitly proven uncompressed subsets documented by the project.
- WIM/ESD and FFU support is bounded container metadata inspection; this beta does not claim image application or mutation for those formats.
- DMG/UDIF support is bounded metadata inspection; unsupported compressed `blkx` decoding is not claimed.
- The physical-media writer remains a hard-gated engineering candidate and is **not exposed in the application UI or public CLI**.
- The public beta asset in this release is Windows x64. An ARM64 project target does not imply an ARM64 beta download.

## Manual release evidence

Interactive release evidence was recorded against the exact package before this bundle could be prepared.

- Manual QA evidence SHA-256: `{{MANUAL_QA_SHA256}}`
- Required observations include clean desktop launch/basic regression, normal-user UAC behavior and real cross-process Explorer drag-out.

